In the dark
You are surrounded by darkness.

> feel
You prod, and conclude that you are surrounded by snow.

> spit
Your drool moves in a direction that you conclude must be down.

> dig
You scratch away in the direction that you believe is up. You keep going until
you finally see light.

Below the cliff
Bright light assaults your eyes. It is snowing from an overcast sky.

So he cut the rope on you. That's so typical of Charlie. He gets all his
knowledge from adventure stories. You've told him over and over: Just because
something would work in a book, it's not necessarily the best way to tackle a
problem in real life.

Still, you suppose he's in the process of learning that now. And you're probably
lucky to be alive.

While you're waiting for Charlie to go and find help, it seems like a good idea
to seek shelter from the elements.

Rock structures block your way in all directions, although you spot an irregular
opening that you might be able to squeeze through. Your landing site, the snow
cave, is below you. The cliff you fell from is towering ominously to one side.
Based on the route the two of you were taking, that cliff ought to be west from
here, which would put the irregular opening to the north.

> n
You climb through the irregular opening.

Cave entrance
You're in a fairly spacious cavity in the mountain, with a large column off to
one side. Bright sunlight enters through a narrow opening in the southern wall,
and there appears to be a passage to the west leading further in.

Wow! Perhaps it's the entrance to a large cave system. Just... wow! Once you're
back to safety, you're going to tell Charlie all about this. He'll be absolutely
thrilled. But you have to wait until you're both back home, otherwise he might
jump into the crevice himself, on a whim.

> tie rope to column
You tie the rope to the column. It is now firmly anchored.

> w
You walk west through the passage. Part of the rope trails after you.

Intersection
You've reached an intersection in the cave system. The walls are rugged here,
full of rough corners and edges. You move slowly so you don't hurt yourself.

This is so cool! Charlie must see this place. He's going to make it into the
setting of one of his stories, for sure.

Passages to the west and south lead into darkness. The exit is to the east.

Your rope, attached at one end to your climbing harness, stretches back towards
the cave entrance.

> s
You walk south. Part of the rope trails after you.

In the dark
It is pitch dark, and you can't see a thing.

> w
Gradually, your eyes adapt to the darkness.

You walk west. Part of the rope trails after you.

Stalactite room
The cave opens up into a fairly large chamber, its floor moist and slippery.
From the ceiling hangs a single, large stalactite, from which water drips
regularly.

There are passages to the north and east. Along its southern edge the wet floor
slopes down to what looks like a perilous shaft.

Your rope, attached at one end to your climbing harness, stretches back towards
the east.

> s
Holding the rope in a tight grip, you carefully lower yourself to the bottom of
the shaft.

In the pit
You're in a pit at the bottom of a shallow shaft. The northern wall curves into
a slope leading back up. High above, you can make out the faint outlines of a
stalactite.

A strong, musty odour emanates from what appears to be a tight crawlway at the
bottom of the northern wall. A larger passage leads east.

Your rope, attached at one end to your climbing harness, stretches back towards
the stalactite room above you.

> n
You squeeze through the crawlway and emerge on the other side. Part of the rope
trails after you.

Dry stream bed
An elongated, curved formation in the floor is dry now, but bears witness of
running water in earlier times. The air is damp and cold, and the musty smell is
almost overpowering in here.

Some kind of fungus grows in patches on the cave walls, emitting a faint blue-
green glow.

The stream bed narrows into a crawlway through the southern wall.

Your rope, attached at one end to your climbing harness, stretches back towards
the pit.

